# The header YOU generate, in step 3 of the exercise.
#
# Note that this is the opposite of what ../../days/*/c-glue/ does: those
# headers are committed on purpose, because they are finished artifacts meant
# to be read (and to work as a fallback when cbindgen is missing). This one is
# machine output from a file that is mostly `todo!()` — it describes whatever
# signature you happened to have when you last ran the script, so committing
# it would mean committing a snapshot of your half-finished work.
#
# The rule is scoped to this directory precisely so it cannot reach the
# tracked headers next door.
/include/

# The compiled C harness lives under target/, which the root .gitignore
# already covers.
